  "name": "Hay bale ring",
  "notes": "Built from Sam's friend's reference photos (2026-11-12), estimated, no measurements given: round bales 1.5 m across and 1.2 m tall, stacked two high (2.4 m). One continuous spiral wall of bales, like a corkscrew: it starts 10.5 m from the centre and draws in evenly by 2.9 m each turn, overlapping itself for about 70 degrees, so the only way in is a curved corridor about 1.4 m wide at the front. Low stage at the back with PA. A standing dancefloor, warm uplights at the foot of every bale, moving beams on top of every fifth bale, low fog from the stage and the sides, two lasers on the bales behind the stage making a liquid sky over the crowd, cold sparks at the stage front. Give one real measurement (ring width or bale size) and everything rescales from it.",
